WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.450
A school near us was given a

2
00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:03.930
box of smart sensors.

3
00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:07.980
A year later, it's still in a cupboard.

4
00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.560
Nobody had asked what

5
00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:12.020
problem they would solve.

6
00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:15.310
Today we start the other way

7
00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:17.130
round: from the problem.

8
00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:20.880
Today: start a smart school project

9
00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:22.900
from a problem, not a gadget.

10
00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:26.600
Start from a problem people feel.

11
00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:29.420
Our water tank runs dry without

12
00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:31.660
warning, two or three times a term.

13
00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:35.380
Ask who it hurts: pupils, cleaners,

14
00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:37.160
the caretaker who checks it.

15
00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:39.740
Talk to them before choosing anything.

16
00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:42.820
Next, turn it into a

17
00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:44.080
question you can measure.

18
00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:47.470
A smarter school is a wish: no

19
00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:48.890
sensor can answer it.

20
00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:51.240
How fast does the water level

21
00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:53.040
fall, and on which days?

22
00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:55.790
That, a sensor can answer.

23
00:00:57.070 --> 00:00:58.730
Then write a success measure:

24
00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:00.430
a number and a date.

25
00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:04.230
Last term, the tank ran dry on five days.

26
00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:07.570
Goal: none by the end of term,

27
00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:08.750
with a day's warning.

28
00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:10.420
Quick check!

29
00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:13.480
A colleague's success measure: the

30
00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:15.220
water problem gets better.

31
00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:16.510
Good enough?

32
00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:19.860
Not good enough: you could never

33
00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:20.900
tell whether it worked.

34
00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:24.760
Better for whom, by how much, by when?

35
00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:28.080
Say: no dry days by the end of term.

36
00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:30.440
Now choose the parts.

37
00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:34.040
A waterproof distance sensor on the lid

38
00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:36.360
measures how far down the water is.

39
00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:39.670
Power: batteries, or a battery

40
00:01:39.670 --> 00:01:41.030
and a small solar panel.

41
00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:44.100
Network: Wi-Fi if it reaches,

42
00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:46.460
a mobile SIM, or LoRa.

43
00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.760
Weigh the options in a decision matrix.

44
00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:52.520
Score each on cost,

45
00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:55.440
upkeep, range and power.

46
00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:59.080
Weight each, multiply and add up.

47
00:01:59.710 --> 00:02:01.530
And agree the weights with the

48
00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:03.790
people affected: the caretaker

49
00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.350
cares most about upkeep.

50
00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:09.200
Count every cost, not just the price.

51
00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:12.750
A SIM's data plan costs money every month.

52
00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:14.510
Batteries need changing.

53
00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:17.180
And someone must climb up to

54
00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:18.740
clean and fix things.

55
00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:22.590
Then put it all on one page: the

56
00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:25.190
problem, question and success measure.

57
00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:28.720
The parts, the cost, and who pays.

58
00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:31.740
A timeline, with a pilot first.

59
00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:34.520
And roles for pupils: builders,

60
00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:37.540
testers, a data team and reporters.

61
00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:39.540
Your turn.

62
00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:41.570
My class scored three

63
00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:43.590
designs, and LoRa won.

64
00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:45.760
Nobody asked the caretaker,

65
00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:47.360
who'll change its batteries.

66
00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:49.090
Is our choice made?

67
00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:53.310
Not yet: the weights are a judgement, and

68
00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:55.150
the caretaker lives with the result.

69
00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:57.640
Ask him, then score again.

70
00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:01.410
Remember: a problem people feel, a

71
00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:04.070
measurable question, a number and a

72
00:03:04.070 --> 00:03:06.510
date, and choices weighed together.

73
00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:10.590
Try it in class tomorrow: a problem hunt.

74
00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:14.730
Groups list three school problems, who

75
00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:17.530
each hurts, and what to measure.

76
00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:20.290
The class votes for one, and

77
00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:21.750
drafts its one-page plan.

78
00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:25.220
Next time: pilot one sensor

79
00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:26.640
before building many.
